  "mechanisms": [
    "Increased levels of cortisol and lower levels of melatonin are related to several diseases.",
    "Plasma melatonin peaks (acrophase) occur 4-6 hours before the acrophase of the cortisol rhythm, driven by the suprachiasmatic nucleus which is sensitive to light exposure.",
    "Melatonin reduces NF-kB activation and immune-competent cell count, while immune system activation interrupts melatonin production.",
    "Corticosterone increases melatonin synthesis induced by \u03b2-adrenoreceptors, suggesting a complex pathway involving the immune system for cortisol and melatonin's influence on mood.",
    "Depression may involve hormonal changes preceding clinical features."
  ],
  "moderators": [],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "Recommending exposure to natural light for workers is reasonable to increase benefits for labor and workers."
  ],
